      "side": 1,
      "message": "This might work when the display is off but I wonder if we could have problems when we turn off display right after we called this?\n\nDo you know which part of the flow exactly prevents `finishDisplayUpdate()` to be called? Maybe we can try to make sure that it doesn\u0027t get stuck there if the screen is off.\n\nAlso, I think we should ensure that we call ready only *after* we update the window hierarchy which happens in `onStartCollect.run()`\n\nAfaik the flow looks roughly like this:\n* DM sends onDisplayChanged event\n* DeferredDisplayUpdater#updateDisplayInfo() is called which calls `requestDisplayChangeTransition`\n* We start collect (or wait for the transition to be started collecting)\n* `onStartCollect.run()` call invokes the lambda that runs `mDisplayContent.onDisplayInfoUpdated` which applies the new display info (e.g. updated size) to all windows\n* We start remote display change with the new display info by sending it to WM Shell and receiving a WCT from it\n* We apply WCT\n* We set the transition as ready\n\nTransitions help us guarantee that changes between starting collecting and making the transition \u0027ready\u0027 are displayed before we continue",
